    <DataNode elementId="AT4G31780-MONOMER" textLabel="UDP-galactose:DAG galactosyltransferase" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="AT4G31780-MONOMER" dataSource="plantcyc" />
      <Graphics centerX="150" centerY="355" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">MGD1 is also known as the type A MGDG synthase. In Arabidopsis, MGD1 and DGD1 are responsible for the bulk of MGDG and DGDG biosynthesis, respectively. MGD2, MGD3 and DGD2 are of conditional importance in glycolipid biosynthesis when the plants are under phosphate deprivation.</Comment>
